WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.911 --> 00:00:09.700 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Welcome to the Africa capitals, episode one of six. First, I clear the chosen
names for a fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:10.364 --> 00:00:19.408 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
We begin along the northern shore of Africa, where the Mediterranean meets the
Sahara, and we end out in the Atlantic islands.

3
00:00:20.069 --> 00:00:22.577 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Tunis into view.

4
00:00:26.946 --> 00:00:36.071 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Tunis stands on the Gulf of Tunis, on the Mediterranean coast of the country
the map calls Tunisia, in the north of Africa.

5
00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:48.845 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The old city of Tunis, the medina, is a UNESCO World Heritage site, and the
ancient city of Carthage stands on the far side of the lake to the north-east.

6
00:00:49.499 --> 00:00:59.693 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Tunis as the modern capital facing Carthage across the same lake,
with Sicily out in the Mediterranean.

7
00:01:00.394 --> 00:01:02.484 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Algiers into view.

8
00:01:09.224 --> 00:01:19.882 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Algiers lies on the Bay of Algiers, the Mediterranean coast of Algeria, west
of Tunisia and east of the Sahara.

9
00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:31.192 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The Casbah, the densely built citadel quarter that steps down toward the
harbour, was inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage site in 1992.

10
00:01:31.845 --> 00:01:38.277 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the white city climbing down to the water: the Casbah above, the
harbour below.

11
00:01:39.013 --> 00:01:41.138 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Rabat into view.

12
00:01:47.164 --> 00:01:56.498 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Rabat sits on the Atlantic coast of Morocco, at the mouth of the Bou Regreg
river, across the Strait of Gibraltar from Spain.

13
00:01:57.163 --> 00:02:08.936 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The Kasbah of the Udayas stands at the river mouth, and the historic city of
Rabat, with that kasbah and the Mohammed V Mausoleum, is a UNESCO World
Heritage site.

14
00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:15.440 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the kasbah at the river mouth, on the African side of the strait,
opposite Europe.

15
00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:18.475 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Tripoli into view.

16
00:02:23.663 --> 00:02:31.674 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Tripoli stands on the Mediterranean coast of Libya, west of Egypt, with the
Sahara stretching south behind it.

17
00:02:32.336 --> 00:02:44.747 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The city grew from the ancient Phoenician settlement of Oea, later a Roman
city of three quarters called Tripolis, and the Red Castle still stands in the
old town.

18
00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:52.087 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the red castle of Tripoli, the Roman three-quarter city above the
Libyan shore.

19
00:02:52.774 --> 00:02:55.282 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Cairo into view.

20
00:03:00.036 --> 00:03:09.591 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Cairo stands on the Nile in Egypt, where the river reaches its delta and the
Mediterranean, with the Sinai Peninsula across the canal to the east.

21
00:03:10.253 --> 00:03:23.256 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The city was founded in 969 beside the Nile and is among the largest cities in
the world; its historic area, with the Citadel and the old mosques, is a
UNESCO World Heritage site.

22
00:03:23.917 --> 00:03:29.966 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the city of a thousand minarets at the head of the delta, with Giza
across the river.

23
00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:33.751 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Nouakchott into view.

24
00:03:37.881 --> 00:03:46.147 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Nouakchott lies on the Atlantic coast of Mauritania, in the dry belt between
the Sahara and the Senegal River.

25
00:03:46.799 --> 00:04:01.985 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
It was a small village until 1958, when it was chosen to be built up as the
capital of the new country; the country’s real harbour, Nouadhibou, lies 400
kilometres up the coast to the north.

26
00:04:02.639 --> 00:04:08.560 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the capital of the sandy shore, with the working port far to the
north.

27
00:04:09.283 --> 00:04:11.280 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Khartoum into view.

28
00:04:17.428 --> 00:04:25.660 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Khartoum stands in Sudan, where the Blue Nile from the Ethiopian highlands
meets the White Nile coming up from the swamps.

29
00:04:26.321 --> 00:04:36.515 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The confluence monument in the city marks that meeting of the two rivers, and
the capital itself stands on an island formed by them.

30
00:04:37.168 --> 00:04:44.030 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the capital on the island between two Niles, the point where the
river is finally assembled.

31
00:04:44.703 --> 00:04:47.431 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Praia into view.

32
00:04:51.992 --> 00:05:00.653 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Praia sits on the southern coast of Santiago, the largest island of Cape
Verde, out in the Atlantic west of Senegal.

33
00:05:01.306 --> 00:05:16.318 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Nearby Cidade Velha on the same island was the first colonial town Europeans
built in the tropics, and the fortress of São Lourenço do Monte still watches
the coast above Praia.

34
00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:25.641 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the Atlantic island capital on Santiago, whose name simply means
beach, and whose oldest town lies just over the hill.

35
00:05:32.372 --> 00:05:44.098 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Tunis faces Carthage across its lake, Algiers steps down to its harbour, Rabat
keeps the kasbah at the strait, and Tripoli holds the red castle above the
Libyan shore.

36
00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:56.430 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Cairo at the head of the Nile delta, the shore capital of the Sahara
at Nouakchott, the capital between two Niles at Khartoum, and the island
capital of Praia on Santiago.
